        "original_id": "e71353c4-d76b-52b6-97de-4fea6b5ea6e0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Platforms: Ford CD2 platform, Mazda GF platform\n- Products: Mazda Capella/626, Mazda Capella, Ford Escape, Mazda Tribute\n- Companies: Ford, Mazda\n\nFacts:\n- Mazda manufactured the Mazda Capella, a mid-size car, from 1970 to 2002.\n- The Ford CD2 platform design is based on Mazda's GF platform.\n- Mazda used the GF platform for the Mazda Capella/626.\n- The Ford Escape and Mazda Tribute share underpinnings constructed from the Ford CD2 platform.\n- The Ford CD2 platform is based on Mazda GF underpinnings in the Ford Escape and Mazda Tribute.\n- The Ford Escape and Mazda Tribute share only the roof and floor pressings as common body panels.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ca96c7ce-543f-56b3-95e5-e8e8efdac37d",
        "text": "Page: Ford CD2 platform. Sentence: The design is based on Mazda's GF platform, used by the Mazda Capella/626.\nPage: Mazda Capella. Sentence: The Mazda Capella is a mid-size car that was manufactured by Mazda from 1970 to 2002.\nPage: Ford Escape. Sentence: Although the Escape and Tribute share the same underpinnings constructed from the Ford CD2 platform (based on Mazda GF underpinnings), the only panels common to the two vehicles are the roof and floor pressings.",
